// [COMMON SUPPORT] Base type for a deployed module's MyBatis Mapper. Intentionally EMPTY.
//
// Same purpose as BaseService — a seam for data-access concerns that should apply to every module without editing
// each Mapper. Have every module's Mapper extend it:
//
//     @Mapper
//     public interface OrdersMapper extends {{PKG}}.support.BaseMapper { ... }
//
// MUST STAY METHOD-FREE. MyBatis resolves every Mapper method against a statement id in the mapper XML, and an
// inherited method is no exception — declaring one abstract method here would demand that statement in EVERY
// module's XML. Add a `default` method with a Java body if you need shared behaviour; add an abstract method only
// if you genuinely intend to require that statement everywhere.
//
// Being an interface is forced, not chosen: a Mapper is an interface, so this cannot be a class.
//
// Only useful with the `mybatis` module_classpath entry selected — that is what puts mybatis + mybatis-spring on
// the host classpath for the module to compile against.
package {{PKG}}.support;

public interface BaseMapper {
}
